"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[53748],{353748:e=>{e.exports='# Discovering & Loading Registered Models (Unity Catalog)\n\nList registered models in a UC schema and load them by alias or version. Unity Catalog\'s registry API differs from the legacy workspace model registry — training-data patterns for the old registry will often fail on UC.\n\n## Listing Models in a Schema\n\n### Databricks SDK (recommended) — server-side filtered\n\n```python\nfrom databricks.sdk import WorkspaceClient\n\nw = WorkspaceClient()\nmodels = list(w.registered_models.list(\n    catalog_name="main",\n    schema_name="my_schema",\n))\nfor m in models:\n    print(m.full_name)\n```\n\nServer-filtered to the target schema, no pagination handling required.\n\n### MLflow `MlflowClient` — unfiltered + client-side filter\n\nUse this when you already have an `MlflowClient` open. The default page size is small, so **paginate** — a single call will miss models past the first page on workspaces with many registrations.\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\nmlflow.set_registry_uri("databricks-uc")\nclient = mlflow.MlflowClient(registry_uri="databricks-uc")\n\nall_models = []\nresults = client.search_registered_models(max_results=1000)\nall_models.extend(results)\nwhile results.token:\n    results = client.search_registered_models(max_results=1000, page_token=results.token)\n    all_models.extend(results)\n\nschema_models = [m for m in all_models if m.name.startswith("main.my_schema.")]\n```\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n- `client.search_registered_models(filter_string=...)` — **`filter_string` is not supported** by this method on Unity Catalog. Filter client-side, or use the SDK.\n- `spark.sql("SHOW MODELS IN <catalog>.<schema>")` — **not valid SQL** on Unity Catalog.\n- `SELECT ... FROM system.information_schema.routines` — **routines are SQL functions, not registered models.** Wrong table.\n- `m.name()` on a `RegisteredModel` or `ModelVersion` — **`.name` is a property, not a method.** Use `m.name`.\n\n## Loading a Model\n\nPrefer alias URIs for champion/challenger workflows — the alias can be reassigned without changing callers.\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\n\n# By alias (recommended for production)\nmodel = mlflow.pyfunc.load_model("models:/main.my_schema.my_model@champion")\n\n# By version number\nmodel = mlflow.pyfunc.load_model("models:/main.my_schema.my_model/3")\n```\n\n## Listing Versions of a Specific Model\n\n`search_model_versions` **does** accept `filter_string` on UC (unlike `search_registered_models`). Note: the `ModelVersionSearch` objects returned by `search_model_versions` do **not** populate `.aliases` on UC — call `get_model_version(name, version)` if you need them.\n\n```python\nversions = client.search_model_versions(filter_string="name=\'main.my_schema.my_model\'")\nfor v in versions:\n    print(f"v{v.version}: status={v.status}")\n\n# If you need aliases for a specific version:\nmv = client.get_model_version(name="main.my_schema.my_model", version="1")\nprint(mv.aliases)  # e.g., [\'champion\']\n```\n\n## Setting Aliases and Tags\n\n```python\nclient.set_registered_model_alias("main.my_schema.my_model", alias="champion", version=3)\nclient.set_model_version_tag("main.my_schema.my_model", version=3, key="stage", value="prod")\n```\n'}}]);
